cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "GISFORUS Spatial Research Suite — Geospatial & Remote-Sensing Analysis Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  An open R / Shiny + Google Earth Engine pipeline for reproducible, publishable
  remote-sensing research: land-cover and change analysis, spectral-index libraries,
  trend and correlation statistics, and a marine/coral module (blue-green bottom index,
  coral-vs-algae variability screen, Degree Heating Weeks, turbidity, Allen Coral Atlas
  masking). It produced the analysis in the companion paper, which uses the 2018-2022
  Maya Bay (Ko Phi Phi Leh, Thailand) tourism closure in a three-tier nested
  before-after/control-impact (BACI) design to show that the reef's apparent post-closure
  "greening" is a region-wide, likely macroalgal signal rather than a closure effect,
  and that a blue-green optical index cannot on its own separate coral from algae.
